#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510508} :activity/id #uuid "238ccd9a-3841-5932-a57b-eab79e3279ba" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050293 :topic/id #uuid "3d717848-5743-5882-aa66-adea2ee38d55" :topic/math-academy-id 1980} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510484 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18541d05-49d2-5f19-b579-6b534b3bcfd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+2y+z+w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435522} {:answer/id #uuid "1e19600e-76b4-5880-a603-02783cbb324e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+y-2z-w+1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435523} {:answer/id #uuid "36b42409-fb4f-52cb-a983-864ab8cc5f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+y+z-w-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435525} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f12775-7dc0-5662-9058-bbd97ad38d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-2y-z+w-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435536} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2e0787-ad3a-5c7f-add5-4e016dc6c7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+2y-3z+w+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435523} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b834ec-93e3-593b-87ef-065fbe59d9c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b798538-8660-5c1f-9d93-5bdad8bdb40c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129477" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=x+y-{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y-{z}^{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y-{z}^{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+y-{z}^{2})=-2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,0,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,1) & =-2(1)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-0 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,1)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,1)+(z-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,1) \\\\ w & =(x-1)+y-2(z-1) \\\\ w & =x+y-2z+1 \\\\ x+y-2z-w+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "124b0422-9a11-52fc-b23f-2b89b132f87d"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92e8db8-6269-551b-aa1e-62c29b8cd052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(0,e,-1)$ and $(1,e,e-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402583} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcaac91-a08d-5d50-b23f-ff424e9006d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(2,1,6)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402584} {:answer/id #uuid "decc010d-972c-5e29-a513-edb14a0563a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,1,3)$ and $(0,1,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402585} {:answer/id #uuid "d5917f2b-570f-54c3-8ea6-d8b9cbf5fbb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(2,-1,1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402586} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4df4a8-f560-557c-ba34-1d929f1ab145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(0,1,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402587}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402584} :answer-field/id #uuid "34dfa067-c400-5022-aa9f-0f008be7be87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "92e52e05-2a21-5219-b9c8-0556f35cdaa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-37982" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=3xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨3,5,-1⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =3y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨3y,\\,3x-\\frac{1}{y},\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨3,5,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨3y,\\,3x-\\frac{1}{y},\\,-1⟩=⟨3,5,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3cy=3 \\\\ 3cx-\\frac{c}{y}=5 \\\\ -c=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n3(1)y=3\\,⟹\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=1$ and $y=1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n3(1)x-\\frac{1}{1}=5\\,⟹\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=2$ and $y=1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =3xy-\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\  & =3(2)(1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector  $v$ at $(2,1,6).$"} :step/id #uuid "593fae8f-a68f-597a-b179-b3261c8ea79e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510558}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510518 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14251a03-b1b0-5ac8-a6b0-8e82d37f60ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+2y+z-2w-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339306} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4ffcc9-fb3a-5477-b6a4-f740f112072a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+2y-z-2w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339523} {:answer/id #uuid "3828bc36-1ffa-5912-9f56-626d879cb2be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+2y-z+2w-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339632} {:answer/id #uuid "76968a25-d5fd-5bfe-851e-0bef52e8fad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-2y+2z-2w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340185} {:answer/id #uuid "87ce18f8-c0ef-5d56-92ea-1b3a22b9548b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-2y-z+2w-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340344}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339306} :answer-field/id #uuid "886a29d7-3a2d-503e-b169-7db643f5c87d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f93b9177-85da-5370-94ac-b27b761710c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73854" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{xyz}$ at the point $(2,2,4,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{yz}}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{xz}}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xyz})=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,2,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 4}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 4}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,4) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 2}}{2\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-4 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,4)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,4)+(z-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,4) \\\\ w-4 & =(x-2)+(y-2)+\\frac{1}{2}(z-4) \\\\ w-4 & =x+y+\\frac{z}{2}-6 \\\\ -x-y-\\frac{z}{2}+w+2 & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y+z-2w-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "78cf1ff6-c2f5-53cb-b4d5-d383c100c0ca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510519}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510519 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e7c281c-3ed2-505e-bb39-624565383d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(-1,1,1)$ and $(2,1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339538} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0e6d85-901c-5c92-bee2-2a7c391f4ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339965} {:answer/id #uuid "92fe27bc-7297-5bff-aa40-85efb366b3a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2,1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340449} {:answer/id #uuid "b73decc5-bf30-5593-9a84-120c9cd31d42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(-1,1,1)$ and $(1,-1,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340784} {:answer/id #uuid "e5166059-3d34-56f7-b88e-8c219479020b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,-1,1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341154}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339965} :answer-field/id #uuid "169b7bd1-0afe-5339-a2e8-b0915ac47bda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9d930cb5-4a33-5f68-a149-002500eed8d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73868" :question/problem "At which points on the surface $z=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector  $v\\,=\\,⟨0,2,-2⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}+2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{x}{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨0,2,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{x}{y}+2y,\\,-1⟩=⟨0,2,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}c\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=0 \\\\ \\frac{cx}{y}+2cy=2 \\\\ -c=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=0\\,⟹\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=2$ and $y=1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{2x}{1}+2(2)(1)=2\\,⟹\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=1$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =(-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-1,1,1).$"} :step/id #uuid "7e867a4e-166b-5049-88c2-c6b51f97a528" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510558 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d287000-354e-5326-9c17-1a60356ce651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-y-z+w-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339249} {:answer/id #uuid "48044e1d-d3aa-5ed8-a17b-609556187f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+y+z+w-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339769} {:answer/id #uuid "89fd8971-4cae-5bee-8c4d-2b478928fdf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+y-z-w+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340360} {:answer/id #uuid "8cbc10d4-f06e-5a6d-b622-4fd3f56ab4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+y+z-w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340391} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6a45f3-ce32-520b-8023-4080f38367c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-y+z-w=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340391} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f40803b-df03-53ae-bb29-eea5e2d21ada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a68ff90-b820-5db0-8c2c-29ec6a4e0d46" :question/math-academy-id "q-73852" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w=\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx}$ at the point $(2,2,2,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{y}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+\\sqrt{zx})=\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{z}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(2,2,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,2) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-6 & =(x-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(2,2,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(2,2,2)+(z-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(2,2,2) \\\\ w-6 & =(x-2)+(y-2)+(z-2) \\\\ w-6 & =x+y+z-6 \\\\ -x-y-z+w & =0 \\\\ x+y+z-w & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ee20eb7f-6214-5a77-9f6d-2cc21ca2637f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510518}}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509679}]}
